From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Li Lingfeng <a1151488180@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0800
Subject: [RFC PATCH 1/2] meta: compact written chunks after an idle interval

Repeated overwrites can leave old slices referenced in chunk metadata
even though the logical file size stays unchanged. Write-side compaction
depends on the mapping record count; below its trigger, covered data can
remain after writes stop if there are no later reads or manual
compaction.

Give these chunks another compaction opportunity after they become idle,
while keeping the existing write-side trigger unchanged.

Keep a bounded, client-local set of successfully written chunks with
multiple records. A single background goroutine checks them after one
minute without a local write, reuses existing compaction and deletion,
and rechecks until clean. It yields while this client has other
compactions in progress. Tracking is session-local; no persistent
metadata format or CLI changes are introduced.

Base: JuiceFS v1.4.1 (0b90c7db5a929ae6adc5faad948d108efd2c99f9)

Assisted-by: gpt 6
Signed-off-by: Li Lingfeng <a1151488180@gmail.com>
